cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ForgeCraft in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ForgeCraft: an open-source framework for manufacturing-aware co-evolution of robot morphology and control"
type: software
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jige0611/forgecraft"
url: "https://github.com/jige0611/forgecraft"
abstract: >-
  ForgeCraft is a Python framework that couples graph-based morphology
  representation, co-evolutionary search driven by a graph neural network and
  PPO control training, rigid-body physics evaluation, and a manufacturing-aware
  export chain that turns evolved bodies into STEP AP242 assemblies, annotated
  DXF drawings, interference reports and bills of materials. Manufacturability
  is treated as a first-class objective rather than a post-hoc filter.
keywords:
  - robot morphology
  - co-evolution
  - reinforcement learning
  - evolutionary computation
  - quality diversity
  - design for additive manufacturing
  - open-source software
